Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:28:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-22: one search box over the whole property grid --
 WPF "Search Properties" (0.22.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Under the panel's header: typing keeps only the rows that have the words --
in every section at once (the editable fields count with the value in their
input, events, web listeners, commands to C++, data fields, DFM properties,
HTML); a section with nothing left folds away, one with a hit opens (also a
folded sub-list such as the computed styles); "找到 N 項" beside it. Words
separated by blanks must all match ("left 54"); Esc clears; the text stays
when another component is selected. The DFM section's own filter became this
box (its old text is taken over). Opening sections for a search is not taken
as the user's choice (the 'toggle' event comes later, the box's text tells).

Tests: panels 5 new checks on the real spbSave data (spbSaveClick: 3 rows,
1 of 8 sections; font.size; "left 54" matches the input's value; no hit says
so; cleared: all 8 back); lib 116, probe, smoke 82, real VS Code 82 -- all
pass; opened files MD5-unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
